{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frail-tsarist-trout","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Make Serena the default path for source-code reference lookup (structural, not exhortative)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`AGENTS.md` §\"Navigating the codebase\" already says, explicitly: \"**Prefer its symbol tools over `grep`** when\nfinding or following references\". During the S2 story of epic `061c-ecd1-8967-4a76` an agent (Claude Code, with\nSerena configured and healthy) enumerated call sites **by hand with `grep`** across several turns and never\ninvoked Serena until challenged by the operator. The guidance was present, explicit, and ineffective.\n\n**Making it more forceful or more verbose is not a candidate fix** — the failure was not insufficient emphasis.\nFour concrete mechanisms caused it, and each needs a structural answer:\n\n1. **Friction asymmetry.** Bash was already in-hand for `rebar`/`pytest` calls. Serena's symbol tools were\n   *deferred* — using them cost an extra `ToolSearch` round-trip to load their schemas. grep cost zero extra\n   steps. Under that gradient the cheap tool wins regardless of documentation.\n2. **Launch-time decay.** `AGENTS.md` loads once at session start. Six review passes into a story, one line of a\n   long document has no salience against what is in working memory.\n3. **No trigger, no feedback.** \"Prefer symbol tools\" is a standing disposition, not a rule bound to a moment,\n   and nothing detects a violation.\n4. **The rule as written is incorrect in an important case, which is corrosive.** Serena/Pyright **cannot**\n   resolve a symbol referenced as a *string literal*. Verified in this repo: `find_referencing_symbols` on\n   `_anthropic_cache_settings` returned the import and all five real call sites but did **not** return\n   `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:90`\n   (`monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"_anthropic_cache_settings\", ...)`). That monkeypatch-string class is\n   exactly what broke story S1's pre-flight (the identical pattern for `_build_retrying_anthropic_model`). An\n   agent obeying \"prefer Serena\" *exclusively* would have missed the site that actually failed CI. A rule that\n   is wrong some of the time teaches agents to discount it all of the time.\n\nAlso observed: Serena's index can lag edits. It reported the cache gate at `runner.py:336` and\n`test_structured.py:175` while the current tree had `:341` and `:176` (a prior commit in the same session had\nrewritten 79 lines of `runner.py`). And grep produced *false positives* Serena did not: two `output_mode()`\nmentions in **comments** (`runner.py:78`, `:160`).\n\nNet: the two tools fail in opposite directions and neither alone is sufficient. The guidance must encode the\ndivision of labour, and the workflow must make the good default cheap.\n\n## Approach\n\nThree independent, individually-shippable changes. None of them is \"reword the guidance more strongly\".\n\n1. **Re-surface the tool at the moment of the action** — a `PreToolUse` hook on `Bash` that prints a short\n   reminder on **every** `grep` invocation. The trigger is deliberately kept as dumb as possible (does the\n   command contain a grep-family invocation) rather than trying to classify \"is this pattern a symbol?\", because\n   a clever predicate is fragile and a fragile hook gets disabled. The message must be **small** (a couple of\n   lines, low context cost) and its job is only to re-surface that Serena exists and is preferred for source\n   references — plus the one legitimate grep case, so the reminder is never wrong.\n2. **Coach it in-band when it is actually missed** — a **project-only** criterion + coaching move so that when a\n   review finds source-code references were enumerated by hand (or incompletely), the agent is directed to\n   re-derive them with Serena. rebar already has the wiring for project-specific criteria and moves\n   (`.rebar/criteria_routing.json` + `.rebar/plan_review_moves.json`); this story either uses it as-is or\n   completes it where it turns out to be missing. Either outcome **dogfoods** the project-overlay feature.\n3. **Remove the friction asymmetry** — make the Serena symbol tools non-deferred for sessions in this repo so\n   using them costs no discovery step, deleting mechanism (1) above.\n\nNothing here forbids `grep`. The aim is to flip the default and keep the exception honest.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.claude/settings.json` (or the repo's hook config) — the `PreToolUse` Bash hook + its message.\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — a new `project.*` criterion, routed via the `activate` map.\n- `.rebar/plan_review_moves.json` — the matching coaching move (`name` / `template` / `applies_when`), plus\n  whatever is needed if code-review moves are not yet overlay-driven.\n- `AGENTS.md` §\"Navigating the codebase\" — replace \"prefer symbol tools over grep\" with the corrected\n  division-of-labour table (see AC3); this is a **correctness** fix to the rule, not an emphasis change.\n- `docs/` — a short note on the LSP blind spot and the stale-index caveat, if a doc home already exists.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Running any `grep`/`rg` through Bash in this repo surfaces a reminder naming Serena's symbol tools; the\n      trigger is a simple grep-family match (no pattern/AST classification), and a test or manual transcript\n      shows it firing on a plain `grep -rn foo src/`\n- [ ] The reminder is at most ~3 lines and names BOTH the preferred path (`find_referencing_symbols`) and the\n      legitimate grep exception (symbols referenced as string literals), so it is never misleading\n- [ ] The hook is **non-blocking** — it never prevents a `grep` from running, and a false-positive reminder\n      costs only the message\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` states the division of labour, not a bare preference: (a) who calls/imports a symbol ->\n      Serena `find_referencing_symbols`; (b) symbol referenced as a **string** (`monkeypatch.setattr`,\n      `getattr`, `importlib`) -> grep, because the LSP cannot resolve it; (c) line numbers after recent edits ->\n      grep on the current tree, because the LSP index can lag\n- [ ] A project-only criterion + coaching move exists such that a review finding \"source-code references were\n      enumerated by hand / incompletely\" emits a move directing re-derivation via Serena; demonstrated by a\n      real `rebar review-plan` or `rebar review-code` run whose output contains that move, attached as a comment\n      on the story\n- [ ] The criterion is scoped to THIS project via the `.rebar/` overlay only — `grep -rn` for the new criterion\n      id under `src/rebar/` finds no hardcoded reference, proving it rides the project overlay and does not\n      change the shipped default criteria set for other clients\n- [ ] Serena's symbol tools require no `ToolSearch` discovery step in a fresh session in this repo, evidenced by\n      a transcript calling `find_referencing_symbols` as the first tool use\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the FULL gating suite (`make test`) pass\n\n## Notes\n\nThe originating evidence lives on epic `061c-ecd1-8967-4a76`'s session log (`535c-cfa2-f06d-4b07`), including\nthe verified Serena-vs-grep comparison on `output_mode` and `_anthropic_cache_settings`. Sample size is one\nsession: mechanisms (1) and (4) are directly evidenced there; the relative ranking of the three fixes is\njudgement, so prefer shipping them independently and observing which actually changes behaviour.","id":"9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["agent-guidance","serena","dogfood"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Make Serena the default path for source-code reference lookup (structural, not exhortative)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785368590884930001,"uuid":"2581a037-6a19-4041-9266-bccdce5a7036"}